{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>For the rain had ceased.</b> Since Moses had not promised him anything except thunder and hail, he said: now Moses is a deceiver; therefore 'he continued to sin.'" "<b>And his heart grew heavy, he and his servants.</b> They said: HaShem does not bring a plague a second time. Another interpretation: since it says above, 'HaShem is in the right,' etc., it implies that it was not in his heart to sin and to hold them back; but now, when he relented, it writes of him 'he continued to sin.' 'He and his servants' — we do not find this expression anywhere else; but because it says above 'you and your servants,' it uses it here. As it says 'he continued to sin' — because it says above 'I have sinned this time.' Thus is the way of the wicked: when they are in distress they humble themselves; once the trouble passes, they return to their corruption. And previously the trouble was upon them, as it is written, 'He who feared the word of HaShem,' etc.; and now, when the suffering passed, they kicked against them."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:56:48.752192586Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}